//An explicit private/protected modifier on an interface member is a
//declaration error: interface members are contract signatures and are
//always public. Rejecting at the declaration replaces the misleading
//call-site error ("does not exist or is not accessible") that a
//silently-private member used to produce.
interface ILock {
    private int secret();
    protected int hidden();
}

int main() { return 0; }
